WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is very exciting.
We were talking backstage.

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:04.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re actually out here not
just to do my show.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you very much
for doing that.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you´re taking
your daughter to colleges.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My daughter Erin and I
did the little college tour

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.811 size:88% position:44%
from Boston to New York,

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:14.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it´s been
a wonderful opportunity.

00:00:14.114 --> 00:00:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
Any parents,
if you have the chance,

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.184 size:84% position:42%
it´s a great time to --

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
great way to spend time
with my daughter,

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:23.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
and figure out
new ways to embarrass her.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that´s nice.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.493
Have you found any good ones?

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:28.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I have.
I´ve got a great one!

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s always been embarrassed
by people recognizing me,

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that´s great.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just, you know,
look like myself.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
That does the job.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:38.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
But also --

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:42.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is because
I´m an older guy, I think.

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:44.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t have time
to figure stuff out.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:47.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want
the world to tell me.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m gonna die.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:51.384
So, we pull in to Boston.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
I roll the window down,
"Where´s Harvard?!"

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:57.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What building
do I have to go to?

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
Give me a name!"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Thank you.
That guy was no help at all."

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, just to strangers,
and she cringes.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:08.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And does that age a person
recognize you?

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:10.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
College kids?
-Most people -- Oh!

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:13.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
College kids
love "Better Call Saul,"

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:15.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
but a weird thing happened
where, uh...

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.910
we were touring one school,

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.146
and we had two fine young women
who were showing us around,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.749
and they were both majors in TV.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.684 size:75% position:38%
One of them knew me.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.253
The other had never heard of me.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.457
Or the show, and I grabbed my
daughter, "We´re out of here!"

00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:32.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Pathetic!"

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You --
I love this show so much.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.031 size:78% position:39%
I feel like it´s such

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
a high level of difficulty
to do this prequel,

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:43.069
and for you, as an actor,
you know this destination

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:45.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
of eventually becoming...
-Saul Goodman.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...Saul Goodman,
who has no morals.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.741
-Yes.
-And you have kind of started --

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.877
Jimmy McGill had some morals,
and they´re sort of eroding.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He´s a good man.
-He´s a good man.

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He starts as
a dimensional character,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then he becomes
one-dimensional.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. You lose --

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
And is it hard
to, like, sort of --

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.453
´Cause it must be a little sad

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
to sort of see
your character lose his --

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.556 size:88% position:44%
-Yes, it is, absolutely.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, in fact,
this third season,

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
which just ended,
and I hope you´ve seen it.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.162 size:84% position:42%
Spoiler alert, I guess.

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
He really takes
a big step forward

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
to becoming this character
of Saul Goodman,

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
who you met in "Breaking Bad,"
and it bummed me out.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I´ve been one,
for this whole time, going,

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Let´s go!
Let´s move this thing along!"

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, when the character
does this thing

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he hurts
this old woman´s feelings

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.283
at a senior-citizen home...

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:33.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
...played by Irene --
character named Irene Landry,

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:37.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
played by Jean Effron,
a great actress,

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he sort of
intentionally ostracizes her

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the other people
at the home.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:47.300
And I called the person
who runs the show, Peter Gould,

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said,
"Does he have to do this?"

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:54.674
And he goes, "Bob, the show
is called ´Better Call Saul.´

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t know
if you´ve seen ´Breaking Bad,´

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you have
to become that guy."

00:02:58.611 --> 00:02:59.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:02.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Yeah, you´re right."

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The other thing
you had to do this year

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.351
that I heard was difficult

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you had to eat
a lot of Doritos.

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah. We had a scene
where I ate Doritos.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, usually,
if you do that on a show,

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.893
they get you
the healthy version or whatever.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
I haven´t had a Dorito
in 30 years.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:18.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve actually
smoked pot more recently.

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:20.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, usually, you would think
those two go together.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But, uh...

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:26.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, uh...

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
I --
They had Doritos.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:31.211 size:88% position:44%
I said, "Sure. I´ll take
a bullet for the show."

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:35.281
And, man, I ate a Dorito,
and my brain exploded.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:40.620
And every single take --
and we do a lot of takes --

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
ended with, "Cut!"

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
and me going,
"Oh, my God, that´s good!

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:46.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:50.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How do they do it?!"
It´s like...

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Applause ]

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:54.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wow!

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.402
I don´t know whether that means

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
you should eat them
all the time

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.473
or you should wait 30 years

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:03.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then eat a bag --
an entire bag.

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:04.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you have any,
like, residual

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:05.945
the next day without Doritos?

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.281 size:75% position:38%
Was that a hard day?
-It was a tough day.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
I cried.
I cried all day.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, now you got
to go another 30 years.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.055
That´s gonna be a long --

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:17.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, congratulations
on your Emmy nomination.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s so well-deserved.
-Thank you.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Truly is.
-Hey, listen.

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:23.263 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:25.865
I just have to say
a shout-out to my cast members,

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
Rhea Seehorn, who´s amazing,
and Jonathan Banks,

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.670
who´s also nominated, wonderful.

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Michael McKean...
-Michael McKean.

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...who this year --
[ Applause ]

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Just...
-Just...

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:38.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don´t --
You can´t be better than that.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Can´t be better.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yet he, sadly,
was not nominated.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.017
I´m gonna call it a snub.
I´m gonna say it´s a snub.

00:04:44.017 --> 00:04:45.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. All right.

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t know why.

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:48.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He´s wonderful.
The show is wonderful.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:49.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you
so much for being here.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really appreciate it.
Bob Odenkirk, everybody!

